;; Proof: swimming (the level-2-2 plan, step 5). FOLDED 2026-10-21 into sparkydave.player.blitz.ab3 and
;; sparkydave.collision.blitz.ab3 with the scaled set as the PAL variant's numbers; kept as the record of the two sets'
;; comparison, its routines renamed Proof... so that it still compiles beside the engine's. The cartridge's water path, written as the routines it
;; will become in sparkydave.player.blitz.ab3, run on the live player code (the includes are the harness's,
;; so the walking, the friction, the vertical move and the collision are the game's own), with two sets of
;; swim numbers for the PAL build to choose between in play (decision 2):
;;
;;   set 0, orange  the PAL listing's: the NTSC numbers, unchanged (JumpMForceData and the rest, entries 5 and 6;
;;                  the surface force $18; JumpSwimTimer $20; the whirlpool's pull $10)
;;   set 1, purple  ours, scaled to 50 ticks a second: forces x1.44, speeds x1.2, the timer x5/6
;;
;; Compiled with the NTSC variant both sets are shown too, but only set 0 is the cartridge there.
;;
;; Keys: LEFT and RIGHT swim or walk, SPACE strokes (a fresh press each time), F1 swaps the set and starts
;; again, F2 starts again, ESC quits and writes the results.
;;
;; The screen is one of 2-2's: the sea floor (rows 13 and 14) with a pit three blocks wide (columns 8 to 10)
;; and its whirlpool (the darker band, a block left of the pit and four blocks wide, as Hole_Empty makes it),
;; a pillar (column 4), a ledge to bump the head on (row 6, columns 13 to 17) and a wall on the right. Mario
;; is the red box; the white line is the water's surface. He starts at the top, as 2-2 starts him, and the
;; pit puts him back at the start. The bar at the top left is the stroke timer (JumpSwimTimer).
;;
;; What to look for:
;;   - before the first stroke he sinks with the area's start force (#MARIO_GRAV_FALL_INIT: $28 NTSC, $70
;;     PAL), afterwards with the stroke's fall force, much slower;
;;   - a stroke lifts him about a block and a half; strokes in quick succession climb, held SPACE does not
;;     repeat; at the surface a stroke does not lift him and he is pushed back under;
;;   - on the sea floor he walks, slower than on land (16, PAL 19, against 24 and 28);
;;   - his head on the ledge stops him (speed 0: the water head-bump fix, both builds) with the bump sound;
;;   - over the whirlpool he is drawn to its middle and down into the pit, and a stroke there is weaker.
;;
;; The results file (proofs/swim-results.txt) has, for each set, seven scripted runs from a standing start,
;; Mario's y every tick (and x for the whirlpool), to check against the cartridge's arithmetic worked by
;; hand: 0 sinking from rest, 1 one stroke tapped, 2 one stroke held, 3 a stroke every 8 ticks, 4 the
;; whirlpool, 5 a stroke every 4 ticks at the surface, 6 a stroke every 8 ticks under the ledge.

OPTIMIZE 1

WBStartup

#PLAYFIELD_PLANES = 4
#COPPER_FLAGS = $10004
#COPPER_COLORS = 16
#SCENE_BM = 2

#SWIM_SET_LISTING = 0
#SWIM_SET_SCALED = 1

#FLOOR_ROW = 13
#PIT_FIRST = 8
#PIT_LAST = 10
#PILLAR_COLUMN = 4
#PILLAR_TOP = 10
#LEDGE_ROW = 6
#LEDGE_FIRST = 13
#LEDGE_LAST = 17
#WALL_COLUMN = 19
#WATER_TOP_ROW = 2
#WHIRLPOOL_LEFT = 112
#WHIRLPOOL_WIDTH = 64
#START_X = 40
#START_Y = 16
#RESTART_Y = 250

#TRACE_RUNS = 7
#TRACE_TICKS = 64

XINCLUDE "/includes/sparkydave.level.meta.ab3"
